ext","text":"The wedge type represents crescendo and diminuendo wedge symbols. The type attribute is crescendo for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"start of a wedge that is closed at the left side, and diminuendo for the start of a wedge that is closed on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right side. Spread values are measured in tenths; those at the start of a crescendo wedge or end of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"diminuendo wedge are ignored. The niente attribute is yes if a circle appears at the point of the wedge,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicating a crescendo from nothing or diminuendo to nothing. It is no by default, and used only when the type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is crescendo, or the type is stop for a wedge that began with a diminuendo type. The line-type is solid if not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specified."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLWedge"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLWedge"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWedge/id":{"type":"topic","title":"id","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge\/id","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies an id reference."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text